WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.042
In this supplied fictional sequence, the normal request

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.316
includes the needed intake details. Show the draft

00:00:06.351 --> 00:00:09.520
summary and the human review point. Complete input

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:13.142
does not itself authorize delivery. Next, show a

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:16.091
request with the delivery date missing. The date

00:00:16.114 --> 00:00:19.284
stays Pending, and the artifact asks a clarification

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:22.521
question rather than inventing a date. Then point

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:26.805
to the absent-approval check: delivery stays blocked until

00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:30.416
a person records approval. Explain what changed after

00:00:30.474 --> 00:00:34.154
testing. The revised version uses written status labels

00:00:34.316 --> 00:00:36.708
and keeps the gate visible beside the output.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:40.493
Open the retained check reference. This is a

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:44.649
labeled tabletop explanation. It does not establish live

00:00:44.696 --> 00:00:49.836
customer delivery, measured savings, or organizational permission. Use

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.588
privacy-safe material and evidence you can actually show.
